# Vector Search

## Mục tiêu

Vector search là kỹ thuật tìm kiếm sử dụng vector representations (embeddings) để tìm items tương tự dựa trên semantic meaning thay vì keyword matching. Trong Cursor Enterprise Framework, vector search được sử dụng cho applications như semantic search, recommendations, duplicate detection, và RAG systems. Mục tiêu của rule này là hướng dẫn developers trong việc implement vector search systems hiệu quả từ embedding generation đến similarity computation.

Vector search enables finding "similar" items even when exact matches don't exist, making it powerful for AI-powered applications. However, implementing it correctly requires understanding of embeddings, distance metrics, indexing strategies, và hybrid approaches.

## Nguyên tắc

**1. Embedding Model Selection**

Choose appropriate embedding model. Consider dimension requirements. Match to content type. Evaluate quality. Consider multilingual needs.

**2. Distance Metrics**

Cosine similarity for normalized vectors. Euclidean distance for geometric similarity. Dot product for recommendation. Match to use case.

**3. Indexing Strategy**

HNSW for high quality. IVFFlat for large datasets. Consider memory usage. Balance speed vs accuracy. Test with real data.

**4. Hybrid Search**

Combine vector and keyword search. Use late fusion or early fusion. Consider BM25. Optimize for both. Test relevance.

**5. Reranking**

Use cross-encoder reranking. Combine with vector scores. Optimize rerank count. Balance quality vs speed.

**6. Chunking Strategy**

Chunk size affects recall. Consider semantic boundaries. Add overlap. Match chunk size to query complexity.

**7. Filtering**

Pre-filter vs post-filter. Impact on recall. Optimize with filtered indexes. Consider metadata indexing.

**8. Evaluation**

Measure recall. Measure latency. Test different configurations. Use A/B testing. Monitor quality.

**9. Scalability**

Design for data growth. Consider sharding. Batch processing. Incremental updates. Cost management.

**10. Maintenance**

Refresh embeddings. Update indexes. Monitor drift. Handle deletions. Maintain quality.

